Code Health
Per-file health scores from complexity, duplication, coverage, churn, and ownership markers, ranked into a fix-next queue, with risk, security, and trend in one place.

Indexed 10/21/2026, 5:24:33 AM · 2bafeccc · 1 snapshot

Health scores changed in this release. Most files score higher: cohesion, duplication, hotspot and complexity findings that did not hold up are gone, and test code no longer counts against production files. Files in languages health cannot analyse used to count as 10.0; they now read "Not analysed" and leave the average, so a repository with many of them can read lower. A repository shows the new scores after its next index, and scores are not comparable to snapshots taken before it.


